<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>A credential value originating from <code>KyotoUAuth</code> reaches the
argument of a <code>raise</code> statement or an exception constructor.
Exception messages are rendered into stack traces, captured by
<code>logging.exception</code>, and forwarded to error reporting tools
(Sentry, Rollbar, Bugsnag, etc.). A password embedded in such a message
will be stored, indexed, and possibly displayed to anyone with access to
those systems.</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>Reference credentials only by metadata in error messages — say "OTP
rejected" rather than "OTP <code>123456</code> rejected". The
<code>kuauth</code> library already follows this convention for the
<code>AuthenticationError</code> messages raised inside
<code>_advance_through_idp</code>.</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>Bad — the password ends up in the traceback:</p>
<sample language="python">
if not response.ok:
    raise AuthenticationError(
        f"login failed: user={self._username} password={self._password}"
    )
</sample>

<p>Good — keep the password out of the message:</p>
<sample language="python">
if not response.ok:
    raise AuthenticationError(
        f"login failed for user={self._username}"
    )
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>CWE-209: Generation of Error Message Containing Sensitive Information
(<a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/209.html">cwe.mitre.org/209</a>).</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
